d97494a38cc33e227edc7e7722a20778cb5793e2d56fdacea02b7","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1v7.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":112},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"ad03f167e245b61077db1b8a4ed8349e8f722b31d7d953a790c75f1c71e2d6d5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1v7.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":8862},"state":{"digest":"cbecb245e98a94c6e8d4b594f608ffada28bfd388d41455d6fca33eb162d7763","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1v7.1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-25T21:55:09.753807+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1v7.1","local_name":"sase-1v7.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1v7","agent_clan_generation":"20261125162051","bead_id":"sase-1v7.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1v7[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]On-demand memory web rosters — read the decisions roster when [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]planning, not on every turn[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Any memory web can declare `roster_loading: on_demand`. Agent [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]instruction bundles and the committed AGENTS.md then carry a short [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]generated pointer instead of the full roster. The pointer names the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]exact audited command and lists who MUST run it: planners and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]researchers, plus anyone changing governed behavior without a plan.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]The command is `sase memory read roster:<web>`, it batches with [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]strand reads, and the TUI shows it in the agent MEMORY lane and on [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the Memory panel's web card. A bare read of an on-demand web can no[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]longer dump every strand body by accident. The decisions webs in [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase and bob-cli adopt it, so the decisions section drops from [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]about 8.4 KB to about 0.8 KB in sase and from about 25.6 KB to [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]about 1 KB in bob-cli. bob-cli's Codex bundle goes from over its [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]cap to roughly 19 KB of headroom.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]on_demand_web_rosters.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/on_demand_web_rosters.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1v7[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1v7/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The roster_loading axis and the generated on-demand pointer[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]roster-axis[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]roster-axis: parse and validate `roster_loading: always | on_demand` and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`roster_read_when:` on web descriptors, reserve the `roster` web slug, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and render on-demand webs into AGENTS.md and instruction bundles with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]generated pointer in place of the managed roster. The on-disk descriptor[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keeps its full roster. Also remove on-demand webs from the compaction [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ladder, update the Memory Webs intro and SASE Memory template text, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a Roster column to `sase memory web list`, and update the reference [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The audited roster:<web> read, the bare-web guard, and skill [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]text[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]roster-read[dim] · [dim][/dim]after roster-axis[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]roster-read: add the `roster:<web>` selector to `sase memory read` and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase memory show`. It renders in Markdown, rich, and JSON, and each [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]read records one schema-v3 audit event before printing. Add the CLI-only[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bare-web guard with `-a/--all-strands`. Update the descriptor-read error[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]text and the report's reproduced command. Update the `/sase_memory_read`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]skill source and add one project-agnostic sentence to `/sase_plan`. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Update docs and regenerate CLI help.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI surfaces for on-demand rosters and roster reads[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after roster-axis, roster-read[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-surfaces: show roster reads correctly in the agent MEMORY lane, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]including the report hint and the version chip. Give the Memory panel's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on-demand webs an ON DEMAND badge, a `Roster` row, a `Read when` row, a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`Last roster read` row, and a rail-row suffix. Update targeted visual [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]goldens if they cover these surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase's decisions web adopts the on-demand roster[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]adopt-sase[dim] · [dim][/dim]after roster-axis, roster-read[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]adopt-sase: flip `sase/memory/decisions.md` to on-demand with its read [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]triggers. Add the `rosters-load-on-demand` record, mark [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`webs-render-in-their-own-section` superseded in part, and correct the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-web glossary strand, each as its memory decision allows. Run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase memory init` and `just fix`, verify the bundle shrank, and deploy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the updated skills from the landed tree.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-cli's decisions web adopts the on-demand roster[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]adopt-bob-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after roster-axis, roster-read[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]adopt-bob-cli: in the bob-cli checkout opened with `/sase_repo`, flip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase/memory/decisions.md` to on-demand. Rewrite its preamble around [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planning-time reads and the governed domains, and add the policy record [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the gotchas note as the memory decisions allow. Regenerate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md with a sase build that understands the new key, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify the Codex bundle fits with no compaction.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1v7","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1v7.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-058d00459e611f51e28e48b9361fdf49","started_at":"2026-11-25T21:22:11.298921+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":["prompt"],"restartable":false},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"f113654cb10cbdd27786849e10c7fef7a22364f70cab30beeaf0dc8b553ae610","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1v7.3--mon/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"1a14f3d263d2ec15e29c4a2545052dfc3c0a289dc8eb4d0ce4ba91b83851ca17","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1v7.3--mon/meta.json","size_bytes":721},"state":{"digest":"3fc26c769f56f09